From 5dc65bb4f5cadbf6a1982dfcf6275aca5ffb0b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Rodionov <fluorescent.hallucinogen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [dxvk] Ask the OpenXR runtime for Vulkan extensions on
 Windows too

The OpenXR extension provider only knew wineopenxr.dll. On Windows, load the
OpenXR loader the application ships next to its executable (openxr_loader.dll),
create a throwaway XrInstance with XR_KHR_vulkan_enable, let the active runtime
name the Vulkan instance and device extensions it needs, and destroy the
instance again before the application creates its own. Extensions the loader /
GPU do not offer are dropped instead of failing vkCreate{Instance,Device}.

This is what the OpenVR provider does through openvr_api.dll; VR mods that
moved from OpenVR to OpenXR (Far Cry VR) no longer get their external memory /
semaphore / fence extensions from SteamVR's compositor, and without them the
OpenXR session on dxvk's device cannot be created. DXVK_OPENXR=0 turns the
Windows path off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TWsKJPmuvTXK3Vo9GTKHQd
